  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"1059\" data-end=\"1229\">\n<p data-start=\"1061\" data-end=\"1229\"><strong data-start=\"1061\" data-end=\"1081\">Positive Result:</strong> Indicates IgE sensitization to Rifampicin &mdash; patient may be at risk for immediate hypersensitivity reactions (e.g., rash, urticaria, anaphylaxis).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1230\" data-end=\"1413\">\n<p data-start=\"1232\" data-end=\"1413\"><strong data-start=\"1232\" data-end=\"1252\">Negative Result:</strong> No IgE-mediated sensitization detected; however, <strong data-start=\"1302\" data-end=\"1332\">non-IgE mediated reactions</strong> (e.g., DRESS, hepatotoxicity) are also possible and not detected by this test.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1414\" data-end=\"1526\">\n<p data-start=\"1416\" data-end=\"1526\"><strong data-start=\"1416\" data-end=\"1431\">Borderline:</strong> Clinical correlation advised; consider repeat testing or graded drug challenge if appropriate.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
